  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "06",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m11p06-m11-p06-p10-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6be88e4b24f3dec6ef9ceeca0cc96c1ca5bfa0a62dd6f079074510fe471d6317",
        "2": "c7a968bad04a8e652efbe0fd4a0a99184d4c3363b84b12754df58e4913fecd5f",
        "3": "07749c7779a1708bf6d00744b8e7ebe1a18345f0776b2fb6ddd3326d6f09d572"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p06-aurora-c1-a0479a94d67f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Aurora when you need managed MySQL-compatible or PostgreSQL-compatible compute that scales separately from storage.",
          "text_sha256": "a0479a94d67ff740d2a78fcb54fbdd18ea51373a764946c0c55b2f23a53320a3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a0479a94d67ff740d2a78fcb54fbdd18ea51373a764946c0c55b2f23a53320a3",
          "asset_sha256": "6be88e4b24f3dec6ef9ceeca0cc96c1ca5bfa0a62dd6f079074510fe471d6317"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p06-aurora-c2-a8f894d12923",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The writer handles changes and optional readers serve queries. Each uses the same distributed cluster volume, not an independent database copy.",
          "text_sha256": "a8f894d12923f563ef0912b549215858cab41b83e657e785373e456372453bce",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a8f894d12923f563ef0912b549215858cab41b83e657e785373e456372453bce",
          "asset_sha256": "6be88e4b24f3dec6ef9ceeca0cc96c1ca5bfa0a62dd6f079074510fe471d6317"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p06-015-c1-e9188db241f0",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If reports strain the writer, add reader compute rather than another independent store. The writer and optional readers use one distributed volume across three Availability Zones.",
          "text_sha256": "e9188db241f0677f099ebb8948c0cea4860a1cb5e91876198a02b52b274a81e9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e9188db241f0677f099ebb8948c0cea4860a1cb5e91876198a02b52b274a81e9",
          "asset_sha256": "c7a968bad04a8e652efbe0fd4a0a99184d4c3363b84b12754df58e4913fecd5f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p06-015-c2-e28846fb1d91",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Read capacity and stored data grow separately. Verify engine and version limits before choosing a design; compatibility does not imply identical features.",
          "text_sha256": "e28846fb1d91490ab5baa19cfb380f55dd44e9a509d1da108527d7ff8b13d124",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e28846fb1d91490ab5baa19cfb380f55dd44e9a509d1da108527d7ff8b13d124",
          "asset_sha256": "c7a968bad04a8e652efbe0fd4a0a99184d4c3363b84b12754df58e4913fecd5f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p06-016-c1-ff20f167cfbf",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Storage redundancy and S Q L read capacity solve different problems. Aurora maintains six storage copies across three Availability Zones, not six database instances that answer S Q L.",
          "text_sha256": "ff20f167cfbf42c09d7d7e532ef615f61a98f6a7832d37c239e973b458d2d393",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0ea2a2fefb0358e92921125f9af089cdfc561704e8f0da4ff2f309ea05ba5d27",
          "asset_sha256": "07749c7779a1708bf6d00744b8e7ebe1a18345f0776b2fb6ddd3326d6f09d572"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p06-016-c2-6f995925ac97",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The writer and optional readers connect to the same volume. Readers can add query capacity or provide failover targets, but storage redundancy does not require readers or guarantee a fixed application failover time.",
          "text_sha256": "6f995925ac97798373ed7cfb95c4e11e3e875de279e7405e7a8281027564ae0c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6f995925ac97798373ed7cfb95c4e11e3e875de279e7405e7a8281027564ae0c",
          "asset_sha256": "07749c7779a1708bf6d00744b8e7ebe1a18345f0776b2fb6ddd3326d6f09d572"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "07",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m11p07-m11-p06-p10-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "f67a0aa965d1a82cb5873736f5eaf2d66f6a5735c85f3b0d536e3384b904ffcc",
        "2": "e48b4c415e854c08db5014b687b70db6bbcfe3a2d85b5d065d548a4c6a9665fe",
        "3": "aa311d71fd5209be53583fc6cb55137011faf8c9166c8da76807fb19bad5f217"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p07-017-c1-cdd691ec9a52",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose an endpoint by where connections should land. The cluster endpoint follows the writer; the reader endpoint spreads new connections, not individual S Q L statements.",
          "text_sha256": "cdd691ec9a5264e3f56a803afc55922dbfdbe4a7dbafa6a43baceeea39a3cfa2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7d6bba9586b76731b79b0e1fd02771f0c522e951d0fea02e01473b9e6df9af3f",
          "asset_sha256": "f67a0aa965d1a82cb5873736f5eaf2d66f6a5735c85f3b0d536e3384b904ffcc"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p07-017-c2-849c3208724c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A custom endpoint selects a subset. An instance endpoint stays with a single named instance. If the cluster has no readers, the reader endpoint can connect to the writer, so it is not an authorization boundary.",
          "text_sha256": "849c3208724c9f6ef5c1f37a295b53cb79b5c7681a3e0adb37e7228203b9a7d0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "849c3208724c9f6ef5c1f37a295b53cb79b5c7681a3e0adb37e7228203b9a7d0",
          "asset_sha256": "f67a0aa965d1a82cb5873736f5eaf2d66f6a5735c85f3b0d536e3384b904ffcc"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p07-018-c1-624d0583a701",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For analytics connections that should avoid Reader A, choose a custom endpoint containing Readers B and C. The built-in reader endpoint can still include all three.",
          "text_sha256": "624d0583a70174a5d0cec1c8b785ca353fa192b109c60b807b7f5c45a3ad0adb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "624d0583a70174a5d0cec1c8b785ca353fa192b109c60b807b7f5c45a3ad0adb",
          "asset_sha256": "e48b4c415e854c08db5014b687b70db6bbcfe3a2d85b5d065d548a4c6a9665fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p07-018-c2-5c0f000f3e1b",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If two workloads must not share readers, use separate custom endpoints with non-overlapping members. This is routing, not physical isolation; monitor reader C P U and replica lag.",
          "text_sha256": "5c0f000f3e1b8430a4cc23257e19d6c9ed77265ea22c9ede13410ceb92b2a0b4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1b102f89b676fd6b17d0996986cf72d9f559044e93bf2cb2907c52b92532e994",
          "asset_sha256": "e48b4c415e854c08db5014b687b70db6bbcfe3a2d85b5d065d548a4c6a9665fe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p07-019-c1-54dac9a8e741",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Use Aurora Auto Scaling to add or remove readers as demand changes within your configured bounds. The reader endpoint distributes new connections across eligible readers.",
          "text_sha256": "54dac9a8e741747a4c5d66cb47ff301f41b6e1487b02432878451e6ad248c717",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "54dac9a8e741747a4c5d66cb47ff301f41b6e1487b02432878451e6ad248c717",
          "asset_sha256": "aa311d71fd5209be53583fc6cb55137011faf8c9166c8da76807fb19bad5f217"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p07-019-c2-e7eb808f54ee",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Allow time for new readers and connection turnover. This policy needs an existing reader to supply its metric, and adding readers does not scale the single writer.",
          "text_sha256": "e7eb808f54ee8962e68893b9ea654bf1c9ab4eabc3f25fffd58b6009289267b1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e7eb808f54ee8962e68893b9ea654bf1c9ab4eabc3f25fffd58b6009289267b1",
          "asset_sha256": "aa311d71fd5209be53583fc6cb55137011faf8c9166c8da76807fb19bad5f217"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "08",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m11p08-m11-p06-p10-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "e4c6561da5f645c740fb84aa5869d453b7967a64fa8f87bdaf807e6e35ba7d28",
        "2": "6dc18f97e431cc62082610bc80999651ceabea8751ac3bebee71670a857ea069"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p08-020-c1-ea6869f45c3f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose a log by what you need to learn. Aurora MySQL error logs show engine failures; slow-query logs reveal expensive statements. General and supported audit logs capture different activity.",
          "text_sha256": "ea6869f45c3f9c5c63ff7fc9d6688505e079c36d685fe12f90603b6162d2d866",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ea6869f45c3f9c5c63ff7fc9d6688505e079c36d685fe12f90603b6162d2d866",
          "asset_sha256": "e4c6561da5f645c740fb84aa5869d453b7967a64fa8f87bdaf807e6e35ba7d28"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p08-020-c2-8929263257e7",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Aurora PostgreSQL has its own logging controls. Export supported logs to CloudWatch Logs, verify delivery, and set access, retention, and encryption; verbose S Q L logs can expose values and increase cost.",
          "text_sha256": "8929263257e7b78740bcf346433ef5159ad1d4b0e55a55c5ff4f07f46ba56dc6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ee029646b602bd23fd1a37ed1140210d3a401df9a9b9e85de1939b08c5a876d3",
          "asset_sha256": "e4c6561da5f645c740fb84aa5869d453b7967a64fa8f87bdaf807e6e35ba7d28"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p08-021-c1-fb16dde6fa98",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Find what is driving database load before choosing a larger instance. Use CloudWatch Database Insights to identify dominant waits and high-impact S Q L, then correlate with metrics and logs.",
          "text_sha256": "fb16dde6fa98349d2e41b3860df447cb1b1191bfc0aa6c32e88149610e41043a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "af074807c982f121b781b066ed654d8484d6b8929cc0e137a14bd439e0803ea6",
          "asset_sha256": "6dc18f97e431cc62082610bc80999651ceabea8751ac3bebee71670a857ea069"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p08-021-c2-ef546f248042",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If lock waits dominate, inspect blocking transactions. If connections are exhausted, check pooling, limits, and leaks. Use multiple signals to confirm the cause rather than assuming all latency needs more C P U.",
          "text_sha256": "ef546f248042f307797296d47c4f32fa4307d2de94093e374a48d51197d151bf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a511a164be43ea79e4f3a167adc3429709e1643227b508886f0fd675508dc509",
          "asset_sha256": "6dc18f97e431cc62082610bc80999651ceabea8751ac3bebee71670a857ea069"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "09",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m11p09-m11-p06-p10-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "5a9cf589de65ffa1f979bb456c5fa804e51eb9a59436d7ebd9470cef24cb319d",
        "2": "ea0a7819534f90e0cf89b182aa162d721b879fe3cb4ab124cbd0a47368542fbb"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p09-022-c1-0c34da6a842d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use Aurora Serverless version two when instance compute demand varies. The graph shows capacity changing within the configured range while the shared storage persists.",
          "text_sha256": "0c34da6a842ddf20ecee83adc792b316932731669845e7b2e67ab66aa640b6ff",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f46fcf54491502a0175f465061610d780313d5880ed09f4df4dff0e425226246",
          "asset_sha256": "5a9cf589de65ffa1f979bb456c5fa804e51eb9a59436d7ebd9470cef24cb319d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p09-022-c2-caedd1d20c52",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A zero minimum can pause supported configurations after an idle period. Check whether resume latency is acceptable; storage and other applicable charges remain.",
          "text_sha256": "caedd1d20c52c8f220f2299a20895215538ecce559918c49594c87e1748a379e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "caedd1d20c52c8f220f2299a20895215538ecce559918c49594c87e1748a379e",
          "asset_sha256": "5a9cf589de65ffa1f979bb456c5fa804e51eb9a59436d7ebd9470cef24cb319d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p09-023-c1-2d3516544aff",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Choose the R D S Data A P I to execute S Q L over H T T P S without keeping an open database socket in the client. I A M authorizes the call, and Secrets Manager supplies the database credential.",
          "text_sha256": "2d3516544aff3549d3d53fdb2570a210ed4a7f1a46e1342e2e7a5f09bc65d0c9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bbb7832116221bd55dc660c3dc43f83d5626be27b8f818f88af2d3a5afceff45",
          "asset_sha256": "ea0a7819534f90e0cf89b182aa162d721b879fe3cb4ab124cbd0a47368542fbb"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p09-023-c2-17ebc281a482",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Even a select runs against the writer, and database grants still apply. Check deployment support, the one-mebibyte response limit, and transaction constraints before choosing this interface.",
          "text_sha256": "17ebc281a4829045f66bb288c4d06569de1ef3b48b80307f69b05ced6d3cf0fb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "983a52b9fdeb3be5f2135fdf15f5d5ff869485c4ea3b5242c1a598473106dcbf",
          "asset_sha256": "ea0a7819534f90e0cf89b182aa162d721b879fe3cb4ab124cbd0a47368542fbb"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "10",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m11p10-m11-p06-p10-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "98b638c3a2783e1f5ed000989169933df6c3e4d71a658bed7b4e8d989cc2b571",
        "2": "e978bd47fdebdba112c9aacaeceae7d9e7220e75bab2c2cabb0c76bb817ff469",
        "3": "8a88687b29e3bafff345ff66194c41cc780f9b7ae826e05d2da39314ecfc533b"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p10-024-c1-4a8c23c3b2f2",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Aurora Global Database for local reads in secondary Regions with one writing Region. The primary replicates storage changes asynchronously to the secondaries.",
          "text_sha256": "4a8c23c3b2f2be1441637c60c3d96f2ea966473c514aa4dd811fcf6a6518ba99",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4a8c23c3b2f2be1441637c60c3d96f2ea966473c514aa4dd811fcf6a6518ba99",
          "asset_sha256": "98b638c3a2783e1f5ed000989169933df6c3e4d71a658bed7b4e8d989cc2b571"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p10-024-c2-02c64234f79c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For a planned move, use switchover where supported. After an unplanned outage, follow the failover procedure; recent changes may not have replicated. Verify lag and application reconnection.",
          "text_sha256": "02c64234f79cf7ba0c420296a3bead60d517be5c3feeb3347866b4c47293acc6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "02c64234f79cf7ba0c420296a3bead60d517be5c3feeb3347866b4c47293acc6",
          "asset_sha256": "98b638c3a2783e1f5ed000989169933df6c3e4d71a658bed7b4e8d989cc2b571"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p10-025-c1-d8c195b10852",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Use global write forwarding for supported statements from a secondary Region, but follow the arrow to where commit happens: the primary writer.",
          "text_sha256": "d8c195b108528242b2ce71a747b108cf855a5cc623ab988fc53d6f7195da70de",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d8c195b108528242b2ce71a747b108cf855a5cc623ab988fc53d6f7195da70de",
          "asset_sha256": "e978bd47fdebdba112c9aacaeceae7d9e7220e75bab2c2cabb0c76bb817ff469"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p10-025-c2-fae7c323b9f9",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Replication brings the change back to the secondary. Read visibility depends on the selected consistency setting, and cross-Region forwarding adds latency. This is not independent multi-writer operation.",
          "text_sha256": "fae7c323b9f9508409d20e25eab8df80643259f26e592beceb869b9f7afef323",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fae7c323b9f9508409d20e25eab8df80643259f26e592beceb869b9f7afef323",
          "asset_sha256": "e978bd47fdebdba112c9aacaeceae7d9e7220e75bab2c2cabb0c76bb817ff469"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p10-026-c1-81a3b0a90969",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Choose a migration route supported for the actual source engine and version. A snapshot restore starts from a recovery point. An eligible Aurora read replica can catch up before promotion.",
          "text_sha256": "81a3b0a90969d3f8495c221a6d873b8adaab2539ca33bf8f38bcce04730dfb65",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "81a3b0a90969d3f8495c221a6d873b8adaab2539ca33bf8f38bcce04730dfb65",
          "asset_sha256": "8a88687b29e3bafff345ff66194c41cc780f9b7ae826e05d2da39314ecfc533b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p10-026-c2-63c0b1b284fc",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Validate data and application behavior before switching the endpoint. Schedule cutover, monitor the target, and retain the source for rollback. If target writes have begun, reconcile them before returning.",
          "text_sha256": "63c0b1b284fcb276fd5b9876ebedc2e5c861be90edb0fa4f5f00430b47ab1c04",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "63c0b1b284fcb276fd5b9876ebedc2e5c861be90edb0fa4f5f00430b47ab1c04",
          "asset_sha256": "8a88687b29e3bafff345ff66194c41cc780f9b7ae826e05d2da39314ecfc533b"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
